    "gpu": "Intel Arc A770",
    "map": "lqdm1",
    "xr": false,
    "note": "Rendered desktop reproduction on the same machine, not a measurement of headset frame latency. Driver cache was not cleared."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Every switch walks the whole game tree and reapplies filtering to 146 unique materials in this scene",
    "Each measured switch triggers 5 draw-time, 7 surface and 12 specialization pipeline compilations; specialization is background work, not evidence of a blocking compile",
    "26 textures are read back to CPU memory on each normal switch, even when their mipmaps already exist",
    "The helper caches textures/shaders only for a single apply call; settings create a new helper each time",
    "Omitting pixel processing reduces direct CPU work to about 2 ms but leaves roughly 78\u201380 ms to draw completion, confirming a larger renderer cost",
    "The lqdm1 test changes zero ShaderMaterial shader resources explicitly; StandardMaterial3D filtering changes alone reproduce the pipeline churn. Baked-map shader replacement is an additional code path, not the demonstrated cause here"
  ],
